<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>North Korea tests attack drones as Kim calls for 'absolute superiority'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcb1b0c9945e02b5aab554b01542a18a9e5446b832f66af9920b22045ac7825a</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T00:22:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261030-north-korea-tests-attack-drones-as-kim-calls-for-absolute-superiority" /><summary type="html">North Korea has tested attack drones, cruise missiles and rocket launchers at a weapons demonstration, state media reported Friday, as Kim Jong Un called for faster development of military drone and artificial intelligence technology. The tests follow a series of weapons trials and rising tensions with South Korea.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Food safety in India: A challenge for the world's most populous country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c16629e42cdcca88429e05edf2f2fbe00fc73e3eb47fa17861237a4b43f28acb</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T15:15:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261029-food-safety-in-india-a-challenge-for-the-world-s-most-populous-country--d71fe213e3e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261029-food-safety-in-india-a-challenge-for-the-world-s-most-populous-country" /><summary type="html">India's food industry feeds more than a billion people every day. But ensuring that what reaches consumers is safe has become an increasingly difficult challenge. The country has witnessed a rise in cases of food adulteration, with sometimes fatal consequences. As concerns over adulteration and poor hygiene grow, questions are being raised about whether regulators can effectively oversee such a sprawling sector.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong leader apologises and housing minister resigns after fire investigation exposes failures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f802f2bcd25545f9b151f4c4e70c5e6a1cb7990d585a68102f4ddf4a6292f657</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:29:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hong-kong-leader-apologises-and-housing-minister-resigns-after-fire-investigation-exposes-f--adfda34a535a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hong-kong-leader-apologises-and-housing-minister-resigns-after-fire-investigation-exposes-failures" /><summary type="html">Hong Kong Chief Executive John Lee apologised on Thursday for a fire that ravaged a residential tower blocks in Tai Po in November 2025, killing 168, injuring 79 and displacing thousands of others. Housing Secretary Winnie Ho resigned Wednesday for her department's failure to supervise the maintenance work. A three-month investigation into conduct will follow, alongside proposals to criminalise bid rigging in relation to the complex's US $38 million renovation contract.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hello Kitty firm apologises, cuts ties with Japanese spy show after China backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d7f60b21b5fb78c82389d318a93bca50c71d3b9acaceba5c8f1bc1692fb710b</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T09:04:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hello-kitty-firm-apologises-cuts-ties-with-japanese-spy-show-after-china-backlash--4fb6031dd3c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hello-kitty-firm-apologises-cuts-ties-with-japanese-spy-show-after-china-backlash" /><summary type="html">Sanrio, the company behind the hugely successful Hello Kitty franchise, has apologised and ended its commercial tie-up with a Japanese TV drama after Chinese state media accused the show of "smearing China", sparking a social media backlash.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires 'around a dozen' ballistic missiles amid rising tensions with South Korea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0417b46b267d29de2a931138948a0a0dc46f3070c9145eaf5132a8e2f950a77a</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T05:04:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-north-korea-launches-around-a-dozen-ballistic-missiles-amid-rising-tensions-with-south-kore--b8fb6dd944c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-north-korea-launches-around-a-dozen-ballistic-missiles-amid-rising-tensions-with-south-korea" /><summary type="html">North Korea fired around a dozen short-range ballistic missiles off its east coast on Thursday, Seoul's defence ministry said. The North Korean capital Pyongyang has stepped up weapons tests in recent weeks despite South Korea's offer of military talks.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India: Over 180,000 evacuated on east coast as massive cyclone hits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:218c9d0ccab2d6cd6e0fa68d589fb434f9e87ffd5952cd171b7593a429d48fd1</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T11:28:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-india-over-180-000-evacuated-on-east-coast-as-massive-cyclone-hits--19a5510d46e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-india-over-180-000-evacuated-on-east-coast-as-massive-cyclone-hits" /><summary type="html">A 125-kilometer-per-hour cyclone hit the southeastern coast of India on Wednesday, October 28, as authorities warned of localised flooding and the uprooting of power and communications poles. At least 180,000 people have been evacuated, while neighbouring Sri Lanka and Nepal have also issued weather warnings. Camille Corcoran reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Real Madrid apologises to China over Mbappé's Mao Zedong comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00939544506c4b0111d702951fd1ca0f52e9c493a7376fe66362968eb2ed0dbf</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T06:00:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261028-real-madrid-apologise-to-china-over-mbapp_-s-mao-zedong-comments--25ef5f10dfe3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261028-real-madrid-apologise-to-china-over-mbapp%C3%A9-s-mao-zedong-comments" /><summary type="html">Real Madrid apologised to the Chinese people on Wednesday after star striker Kylian Mbappé sparked a furious backlash over comments referring to the founding leader of Communist China as a dictator. The club's apology came a day after Mbappé and Spain's La Liga football championship expressed regret over the remarks.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>As China's Communist Party holds plenum, Xi's anti-corruption drive continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73be6151060fed92c4f47cab29fe935afdaeb2e439b42f04ffee01c2e41f7607</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:16:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261027-as-china-s-communist-party-holds-plenum-xi-s-anti-corruption-drive-continues--b51be6c2b893.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261027-as-china-s-communist-party-holds-plenum-xi-s-anti-corruption-drive-continues" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, we try to figure out what happens behind the closed doors of the Chinese Communist Party's plenum meeting. At the heart of the discussions will be President Xi Jinping's firm grip on power. For analysis, we're joined by Jean-François Di Méglio from the Asia Centre think tank.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Azerbaijan: Rare protests over hijab ban in schools</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3957ff864d6a545a01c554f82dbc81eb850a4f3c22694a8fc0c8778fc4b3bd8</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:16:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261027-azerbaijan-rare-protests-over-hijab-ban-in-schools--72dbcc5dfced.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261027-azerbaijan-rare-protests-over-hijab-ban-in-schools" /><summary type="html">In Azerbaijan, a new government ban on hijab in schools has provoked rare public protests. The ban prohibits clothing deemed "incompatible with the secular principles of general education". While it does not mention Islamic hijab, girls and teachers wearing hijab have been turned away from schools. The measure has sparked tensions in a country where 96% of the population is Muslim.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Typhoon Champi batters Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fbc97fee6bd22416e374dfd705ec4bf9e2437b443bcb8f95e95f456f4bcd942</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan--3f52c552700e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan" /><summary type="html">Typhoon Champi is heading towards China and Japan. Yesterday, it battered Taiwan with heavy rain and winds reaching up to 180 kilometres per hour. Across the island, 56,000 households are without power. Nicolas Chamontin and Ophelie Jacobson report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why do women in public life become targets?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0a07abb33f86b7dba91c7a01228caf42422e71d0d35a6ebce00fd315b0e615</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:58:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261023-why-do-women-in-public-life-become-targets--350d0cae4873.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261023-why-do-women-in-public-life-become-targets" /><summary type="html">A brutal targeted attack on an Australian female MP, who lost both her legs as a result, has reignited concerns over the rising levels of violence against women in public life. Also Cornell University is facing a no-confidence vote over its handling of an alleged gang rape in 2024. Annette Young speaks to Annie E. Clark, a survivor of campus sexual assault and Dr Sara Wilf of George Mason University about why institutions continue to struggle with sexual assault cases.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Singapore's longevity industry: The quest for eternal youth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef07c3950021401f893669aff5fc3cdacad73974e354558a6a2e33b70fd8b4de</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:53:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth--7654b61f92cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth" /><summary type="html">In Singapore, the quest for eternal youth is no longer just a billionaire's fantasy. It's becoming big business. High-tech clinics, longevity labs and specialist companies all promise the same thing: slowing down the ageing process. From continuous metabolic monitoring and genetic testing to supplements and oxygen therapy, every aspect of the body is measured and optimised.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan shuts down schools and businesses as Typhoon Champi approaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23bd2a28bdfa77c74974527d2dbf34223fb014f01207c66c195ac3213994b24f</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T03:00:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261023-taiwan-shuts-down-schools-and-businesses-as-typhoon-champi-approaches--0f72f77296ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261023-taiwan-shuts-down-schools-and-businesses-as-typhoon-champi-approaches" /><summary type="html">As Typhoon Champi approached Taiwan, most businesses and schools were closed across the island Friday and hundreds of flights were canceled in the region. Authorities reported at least one death and dozens of injuries and more than 1,200 people have evacuated their homes.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Strong earthquake strikes China’s remote Tibet region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:504b68486d2e350798c61f66973cf3845f96cf34743898e4956704628ec5182c</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T21:09:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261022-many-dead-massive-earthquake-strikes-china-s-remote-tibet-region-magnitude-seven--9ae8ceb17977.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261022-many-dead-massive-earthquake-strikes-china-s-remote-tibet-region-magnitude-seven" /><summary type="html">At least 16 people have died and dozens more injured after a major earthquake measuring 7.0 on the Richter scale shook China’s remote Tibet region on Thursday, state media said. Hundreds of houses collapsed in the tremor.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Dalai Lama appointed by China 'is going to be a fake one', exiled former Tibetan leader says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d6e6b426fd4d8c5484f089d5bf20c20ed8ce57dd3dc17473015e21f163b9a4c</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T10:22:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261022-dalai-lama-appointed-by-china-is-going-to-be-a-fake-one-exiled-former-tibetan-leader-says--f8e9f1f22fcf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261022-dalai-lama-appointed-by-china-is-going-to-be-a-fake-one-exiled-former-tibetan-leader-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, exiled former Tibetan leader Lobsang Sangay said any successor to the Dalai Lama appointed by China "is going to be a fake one". He also likened Beijing's ethnic unity law to "an ethnic erasure", said Tibetan concerns had been "downgraded a bit" in US-China talks and accused China of failing to warn of the deadly August floods on the Nepal-Tibet border.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia continues to battle wildfires, with nearly 2 million hectares burned</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff698cff3f6f9c579ab57e2570e925b8fd3e31350c21a93e41bbe23b22093016</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T10:23:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261020-indonesia-continues-to-battle-wildfires-with-nearly-2-million-hectares-burned--5514d17d6fb8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261020-indonesia-continues-to-battle-wildfires-with-nearly-2-million-hectares-burned" /><summary type="html">Fires in Indonesia have burned through more than 1.9 million hectares of land, according to new data, as the country battles its worst wildfire season in a decade. The blazes have sent toxic smoke across much of Southeast Asia, forcing schools to close and fuelling a rise in respiratory illnesses. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Driver charged over 'targeted' car attack on Australian lawmaker Helen Haines</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20fdc5006676594d178166fb40d82c4ee77936791868d276dae8d5515b08357f</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T02:39:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261020-driver-charged-over-targeted-car-attack-on-australian-lawmaker-helen-haines--a831b000d15c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261020-driver-charged-over-targeted-car-attack-on-australian-lawmaker-helen-haines" /><summary type="html">Police on Tuesday charged a driver with intentionally causing serious injury to Australian federal lawmaker Helen Haines, who is in a critical condition after being struck by a car outside her office in an incident that has shocked the nation. Haines had her leg amputated following the attack, according to Australian media reports.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Months-long Indonesia wildfires spew toxic haze across Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c43a2d94c13f5b07af84f89d0c9ab95081f25810cd99ad6c448bcfdd5b0c3fd</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T06:30:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-months-long-indonesia-wildfires-spew-toxic-haze-across-southeast-asia--f065858c7f80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-months-long-indonesia-wildfires-spew-toxic-haze-across-southeast-asia" /><summary type="html">Parts of southern Southeast Asia have been put under the highest-level haze alert as wildfires that have swept Indonesia for months continue to belch toxic smoke across the region. The seasonal wildfires are worse this year due to the drought conditions caused by a severe "super-El Nino" effect.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India's 'cockroach' movement founder released from police custody</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6798c465144c894f066991f6d9fba27069331fb480bb67c2376e06e435753d73</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T05:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-india-s-cockroach-movement-founder-released-from-police-custody--284536488984.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-india-s-cockroach-movement-founder-released-from-police-custody" /><summary type="html">Indian police released Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke from detention on Saturday after the activist was detained ahead of a rally calling for the resignation of India's chief election commissioner. Two other CJP leaders remain in custody after having been arrested while demonstrating at a protest site that police had ruled off-limits.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's forest fires spark public health crisis across Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddfe10bc4af9783f7f192bbf945e09f38c6fb35b11bc735bec4ec11305913f72</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:26:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261016-indonesia-s-forest-fires-spark-public-health-crisis-across-southeast-asia--ce92433485e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261016-indonesia-s-forest-fires-spark-public-health-crisis-across-southeast-asia" /><summary type="html">Massive wildfires in Indonesia show no sign of letting up. The environmental disaster is turning into a pollution crisis across Southeast Asia, as toxic haze from the blazes spread to neighbouring countries.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Indian authorities detain 'cockroach' movement founder Dipke ahead of new protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e43fec6473533c65426b2fb44d6f739e6dc07647db6555bef3593c613fafd888</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:39:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261016-indian-authorities-heighten-security-close-park-ahead-cockroach-movement-rally--7b06e6dcb92a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261016-indian-authorities-heighten-security-close-park-ahead-cockroach-movement-rally" /><summary type="html">Indian authorities on Friday detained Abhijeet Dipke, the founder of the satirical youth movement "Cockroach Janta Party", ahead of a new protest in New Delhi, live images from the group showed. Police earlier closed a central New Delhi park in an attempt to stifle near-daily demonstrations calling for the election authority chief's resignation over the removal of more than 130 million people from voter lists.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan school roof collapse kills dozens of pupils, teacher in Peshawar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6d5e0aa906deb89b908610db369beea76eb4c9aa747fddb7122cd774e1c623d</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:02:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261015-pakistan-school-roof-collapse-kills-dozens-of-pupils-teacher-in-peshawar--9a905ed0517b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261015-pakistan-school-roof-collapse-kills-dozens-of-pupils-teacher-in-peshawar" /><summary type="html">A teacher and at least 32 pupils were killed when a school roof collapsed in the northwestern Pakistani city of Peshawar on Thursday, authorities said. At least twenty people were injured, three of them severely.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea test-fires submarine-launched cruise missiles amid rising tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8104b99040cdc8bd4014a757b4af81e660204cd51684f229fd7a77f20ac9966f</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T23:12:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-north-korea-test-fires-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles--e31421af3b62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-north-korea-test-fires-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles" /><summary type="html">North Korea test-fired two types of submarine-launched strategic cruise missiles on Wednesday, state media KCNA reported Thursday, saying the launches posed no threat to neighbouring countries. The tests follow heightened tensions with South Korea after a September 21 landmine explosion in the Demilitarised Zone injured three South Korean soldiers.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>How far will 'Cockroach' movement go? India's youth-led protests defy Modi government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d9abb29c0ea1cba8675f86bb3fb25c9b3b303834517cf5f58fef245adbf569b</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T18:40:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government--26fd7d79299c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government" /><summary type="html">It all started as a bit of online satire by a few young people fed up by corruption. Clearly though, the "Cockroach" movement is no longer a laughing matter for India’s government, which has shut transport and blocked rallying points in the capital to quell the momentum of a youth-led mobilisation that's already brought down the education minister over rampant school exam cheating and is now spearheading the protests against the culling of names from voter rolls, with the electoral commission chief accused of bias.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>‘The idea that Modi must be feared because he holds all levers of power has gone out of the window’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20fd55295f0b8313406ef5dd799e99f0032b167c348bceab249312cdbfe9a947</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T16:51:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window--88dfae3f38b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window" /><summary type="html">Is Narendra Modi losing his most powerful political asset: the perception of invincibility? As India's youth protest movement confronts an increasingly combative government, Dr. Subir Sinha, Director of the SOAS South Asia Institute and Reader in Development Studies, argues that the political significance of the demonstrations extends far beyond the arrests of opposition activists and the growing confrontation between protesters and state institutions. Dr. Sinha examines how the government's increasingly repressive response may be exposing the fragility of its authority and institutional legitimacy. Could India's emerging protest movement be dismantling the political mythology that has sustained Modi's hold on power?</summary></entry><entry><title>Cheap weapons, growing fears: Inside the Taliban’s drone campaign against Pakistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dcb0535763549365e800552b62d27790afcaa0bcaaefb4d05bf04fe5866533f</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T12:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-taliban-suicide-drone-attacks-pakistan--4d38ee0ab100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-taliban-suicide-drone-attacks-pakistan" /><summary type="html">Pakistan says it intercepted 23 suicide drones launched from Afghanistan into Pakistani airspace in September alone. Since the conflict began in February 2026, the Taliban have increasingly used drones to attack Pakistan, raising concerns in Islamabad.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>‘Dark day for Turkey’: Police halt broadcasts, make arrests in raid on opposition TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a405b588b0d23559a12c9fc8b85730261db8390700b075c2d3d3c05d11daeb60</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:09:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-pro-opposition-tv-channel-boss-slams-police-raid-broadcast-halt--2027488a6f87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-pro-opposition-tv-channel-boss-slams-police-raid-broadcast-halt" /><summary type="html">Turkish authorities appointed a government trustee to run popular broadcaster Halk TV on Wednesday after police raided its headquarters, halting live broadcasts and arresting 11 people. Halk chairman Cafer Mahirogluin denounced "a dark day for Turkey", adding that seven of his family members were among those detained.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Asia's fertility hub: Thailand emerges as top destination for IVF treatment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ca7f9cb0b03cfadbf69522005c25bbf1d59f3de0ac1b3bbc60a8e36a49ad91c</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T12:38:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261013-asia-s-fertility-hub-thailand-emerges-as-top-destination-for-ivf-treatment--bc3bbfd133c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261013-asia-s-fertility-hub-thailand-emerges-as-top-destination-for-ivf-treatment" /><summary type="html">Thailand has become one of Asia's leading fertility hubs. Every year, thousands of foreign patients travel to Bangkok's state-of-the-art private clinics for IVF, egg donation and other fertility treatments. They come from China, South Korea, Europe and across Southeast Asia, looking for what may be harder to find at home: shorter waiting times, lower costs and, in some cases, fewer restrictions.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>India’s youth-led Cockroach movement defies protest ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95bacd25a7581b348482d7df532b53353af75bd01dc4abb7ddfbc115ef7d606e</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:00:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-defies-protest-ban--510cf1269e48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-defies-protest-ban" /><summary type="html">India’s youth-led Cockroach movement is intensifying protests against Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government. Three leaders were detained after defying a ban at New Delhi’s Jantar Mantar protest site. Demonstrators are challenging a voter-list revision they claim favours Modi’s party, while the protests disrupt businesses across the capital.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands of Indians march to Supreme Court to oust election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:613c64395086f8477aca13995ca5d83cfd10c6be2aa2f8648bad87a73ce115c2</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:23:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief--cfcf565f6afb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Protesters in New Delhi continue to take to the streets demanding the country's top election commissioner resign. Frustrations have been mounting after an investigation in a leading newspaper revealed concerns had been raised within the body, over the revision of voter lists. Delano D'Souza reports.</summary></entry></feed>
